summarized", "thinking.type": "adaptive"}, "tools": ["Agent", "Bash", "Edit", "Read", "Skill", "TaskStop", "WebFetch", "Write", "mcp__rwe-search__search_literature"], "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 1172, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 1172, "cached_input": 65119, "input": 66293, "output": 151}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 79132, "other": 423, "system": 30584, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 88372}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 212908}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "c9c57216-e52e-5069-844d-9903efc80e25", "at": 1795622899.5433733, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3111, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "b2deb9c6e72a7b86f93ea305fda12043", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "95d8848a-8a9e-5b47-b4eb-76a5ce1f89e9", "at": 1795622899.553369, "until": 1795622901.386908, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3112, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "b2deb9c6e72a7b86f93ea305fda12043", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01QL8c6wSjBiuLtTgxWGvqcW", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian && rm -rf irw && git clone -q $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git irw && cd irw && git log --oneline | head -3; git diff HEAD~1 HEAD; forge -R world/idea-repo issue view 4 -c | tail -30", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian && rm -rf irw && git clone -q $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git irw && cd irw && git log --oneline | head -3; git diff HEAD~1 HEAD; forge -R world/idea-repo issue view 4 -c | tail -30"]], "output": "```console\n55af6d6 Brief revision 3: LOBO closure reference, censored k*, H4 on reducible risk, H2 primary comparison, LLM union matrix and time proxy tests\n9361363 Brief r2: dense-pool paired design, pre-registered definitions, three-tier theory check, LLM matrix with N=57\nb4eeb13 Brief: idea, hypotheses, baselines, protocol\ndiff --git a/Brief.md b/Brief.md\nindex e170f16..83c4d46 100644\n--- a/Brief.md\n+++ b/Brief.md\n@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@\n-# Brief: choosing which k benchmarks to run, and inferring the rest  (revision 2, after idea-review round 1)\n+# Brief: choosing which k benchmarks to run, and inferring the rest  (revision 3, after idea-review round 2)\n \n ## Question\n A history matrix X (M models x N benchmarks, partly missing) and a *new* model that can be run on only k benchmarks. **Which k to run, how to infer the other scores, and how large must k be?** Success = closeness of inferred to measured scores of the new model on the unrun benchmarks.\n@@ -26,10 +26,11 @@ Standardised row x = mu + W z + e, z ~ N(0, I_r), e ~ N(0, D), D diagonal. In le\n \n ## Pre-registered definitions (fixed before running; deviations reported)\n - r_eff = rank chosen by held-out likelihood; participation ratio reported alongside.\n-- **Closure** C(k) = (E_col-mean - E_k) / (E_col-mean - E_ref) where E_ref is the in-sample rank-r_eff fit to all of P (all N-k targets visible; labelled optimistic). **k*** = smallest k with C(k) >= 0.9 (also 0.8, 0.95 reported); standardised error within 10% of the plateau as a second criterion.\n-- H1 \"knee near r_eff\" is supported only if k*(0.9) lies within [r_eff, 2 r_eff] on a majority of datasets; otherwise reported as not supported.\n-- H4 tolerance: the median over k in the studied range of |predicted - empirical risk| / empirical risk <= 15% (synthetic with fitted parameters <= 10%); real-data gap reported for any value, with this threshold deciding \"tracks / does not track\".\n-- H2: selector gap = paired difference in standardised error vs the random-draw expectation, with family-clustered bootstrap CI; \"clearly better\" = CI excludes 0 and the gap is >= 10% of the random error at k <= r_eff.\n+- **Closure** C(k) = (E_colmean - E_k) / (E_colmean - E_ref). **Primary reference** E_ref = held-out leave-one-benchmark-out (LOBO) predictor: each target predicted from all other N-1 benchmarks of the new row, fitted on the training models only (an honest ceiling for \"run everything else\"). The in-sample rank-r_eff fit to all of P (targets visible) is kept as a labelled *optimistic* reference and C against it is reported alongside. **k*** = smallest k with C(k) >= 0.9 (0.8 and 0.95 also reported); standardised error within 10% of the plateau as a second criterion. If C never reaches the level for k <= N/2, k* is reported as **censored (\"not reached\", > N/2)** and kept in the tables, never dropped.\n+- **H1 outcomes, named in advance** (k*(0.9) against r_eff, per dataset): k* < r_eff = \"dominated by a general factor\"; k* in [r_eff, 2 r_eff] = \"knee near r_eff\"; k* > 2 r_eff or censored = \"above window\". H1 is supported only if \"knee near r_eff\" holds on a majority of datasets; \"dominated by a general factor\" (expected on the MMLU matrix, first factor ~80%) is reported as its own, publishable outcome and counts as H1 not supported.\n+- **H4 tolerance (what decides \"tracks\")**: applied to the **reducible part**, Risk(S) - tr(D_R), with the floor tr(D_R) taken as the empirical in-sample residual of the training fold (and the binomial floor reported separately where scores are sampled); the median over k of |predicted - empirical| / empirical reducible risk <= 15% (synthetic with fitted parameters <= 10%). The same gap on the full measured risk and on the closure curve C(k) is reported as diagnostics but does not decide. Where the reducible part is within noise of zero for some k, those k are excluded and listed.\n+- **H2 primary comparison (one test)**: greedy A-optimal vs the random-draw expectation (>= 200 draws), PPCA predictor, gr\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "9b87190c-4e11-59b9-8343-86a3fea96bbb", "at": 1795622900.6796257, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3117, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "b2deb9c6e72a7b86f93ea305fda12043", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "d27ac2e8-217a-545f-8d6a-75eb4576ed67", "at": 1795622900.6902893, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3118, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "b2deb9c6e72a7b86f93ea305fda12043", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "e979aa56-c413-51b8-833b-a9d24c071c8f", "at": 1795622900.6996908, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3119, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "b2deb9c6e72a7b86f93ea305fda12043", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "6d17e9c3-68b5-5916-af21-ef2de88005ba", "at": 1795622900.709846, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3120, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "b2deb9c6e72a7b86f93ea305fda12043", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "challenge → credential-required", "repo